@startuml refund-sequence
title Google Play IAP - refund / chargeback handling
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor       Player
actor       "Support /\nDeveloper"               as Dev
participant "Google Play"                         as Play
queue       "Pub/Sub\n(RTDN topic)"               as PubSub
participant "API\n/api/google/rtdn"               as API
participant "Refund job\n(daily)"                 as Job
database    "PostgreSQL"                          as DB
participant "Google Play\nDeveloper API"          as GApi

== A. Something voids the purchase ==
alt Player requests refund (~48h, Play Store)
    Player -> Play : Request refund
else Developer refunds (Play Console order management)
    Dev -> Play : Refund order
else Bank chargeback / Google fraud action
    Play -> Play : Void purchase
else Not consumed within 3 days
    Play -> Play : Auto-refund + revoke
end
Play -> Player : Money returned

== B. Real-time notification ==
Play -> PubSub : voidedPurchaseNotification\n{purchaseToken, orderId, refundType}
PubSub -> API : HTTPS push (OIDC JWT from Pub/Sub)
API -> API : Verify Pub/Sub JWT + packageName
API -> DB : Find transaction by purchaseToken
alt Not found or already Refunded
    API --> PubSub : 200 OK (ack, nothing to do)
else Found (Purchased)
    group Single DB transaction
        API -> DB : state = Refunded,\nstore voidedSource / voidedReason / voidedAt
        API -> DB : Reverse granted rewards\n(ledger entry: -1000 gems, balance may go negative)
        API -> DB : refund_count++ for user;\nflag account if over threshold
    end
    API --> PubSub : 200 OK (ack)
end
note right of PubSub : Non-2xx -> Pub/Sub retries.\nHandler must be idempotent.

== C. Reconciliation (catches missed notifications) ==
Job -> GApi : voidedpurchases.list(startTime = last run - overlap)
GApi --> Job : voidedPurchases[] {token, orderId, voidedSource, voidedReason}
loop each voided purchase
    Job -> DB : Same idempotent refund logic as step B
end

== D. Player next opens the game ==
Player -> API : Login / get wallet
API --> Player : Balance (may be negative)\n+ message about reversed purchase
note right of Player : Policy choice: block spending until balance >= 0,\nor restrict purchases / ban after repeated refunds.
@enduml
